WEBVTT
 
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.000
Anything you want to say to players
who might not have tried the mode yet?
 
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:05.000
Stay away if you don't like fun.
 
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:09.500
[laughter] No, I'm kidding.
Don't put that in there.
 
00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:14.000
The idea for Gauntlet Glitched came from
all the player fantasies and things we'd wanted
 
00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:18.000
to do with agents in the past
and just really couldn't. So,
 
00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:22.000
finding a way to have a release valve
to be a lot more creative
 
00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:26.000
and try the things we might try in a prototype
but wanted to try in a
 
00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:29.500
more competitive sense, right? What does it look like
if we're using three different abilities
 
00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:34.000
from three different agents against other people
in a 2v2 skirmish style
 
00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:38.000
and we got a little team together for our Thunderdome
and just kind of built it out.
 
00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:43.000
Thunderdome is a three-day hackathon that Riot hosts
every year, where devs can get together
 
00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:47.000
with their friends, form a team
and make a quick
 
00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:51.000
game project in under 72 hours. We were able to put
a really fun first playable together
 
00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:54.000
and we host a lot of playtests
 
00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:58.000
during those three days leading up
to the science fair.
 
00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:02.000
It's a 2v2v2v2, so it's like eight people.
We had eight PCs set up.
 
00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:05.500
People were jumping in. A lot of people were like,
"What the... is going on?"
 
00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:08.500
I guess being able to be creative
was kind of neat for a lot of people.
 
00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:11.000
It was a lot of excitement and joy,
a lot of screaming.
 
00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:14.500
Yo. Oh, that was such a sick idea.
 
00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:19.000
All of us who were on the floor playtesting
knew there was something really promising.
 
00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:22.000
This was also right around the time
that we were working on Skirmish,
 
00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:26.000
right? And so Skirmish was coming out,
that was also a 2v2 dual mode,
 
00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:30.000
and Ability Draft almost felt like the next level of that
and they were already prototyping it, and
 
00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:34.000
we were like, "Oh wow, this is really awesome."
 
00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:39.000
And a really telling sign was hearing people on the floor
asking where they could play the mode.
 
00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:45.000
You see people keep playtesting it
after the Thunderdome period, after the science fair.
 
00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:49.000
Dev keeps fixing the bugs after the Thunderdome as well.
And that's when you know like,
 
00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:53.000
"Oh, there's something to chase there."
Nice bumbas.
 
00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:56.000
That was so big. [laughter]
 
00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:59.500
Shortly thereafter, we had the year planning
for what we were going to do in 2026.
 
00:01:59.500 --> 00:02:02.000
And so, knowing that
 
00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:06.000
we had a really promising game mode and play pattern,
and we were going to focus on game modes this year,
 
00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:08.500
we were like, "Okay, let's do this thing,
 
00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:11.000
and this will probably be the climax
of all the game modes that we release."
 
00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:14.000
The next-step challenge for us was
how to inject more depth.
 
00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:17.000
It started out with only eight people,
and we
 
00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:22.000
went to eight teams. So we had a 2v2v2v2,
but now it's like 2v2v2v2v2v2v2v2.
 
00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:26.000
So 16 players added a ton of depth.
 
00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:29.500
And then the abilities themselves,
we only had like seven abilities per—
 
00:02:29.500 --> 00:02:32.000
I don't think we even had ultimates.
Maybe we had ultimates.
 
00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:36.000
So what if, you know, a Wingman is bigger
and with more health?
 
00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:40.000
What if Skye's dog actually kills you in one bite?
And we
 
00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:44.000
ended up with this list of, you know, the crazier branch.
And the list just kept getting longer and longer.
 
00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:48.000
And we were like, well,
there has to be a
 
00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:52.000
systemic way where we can put this list
of special branch into the game.
 
00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:56.000
And that's when we came up with this idea
of Glitched as a theme.
 
00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:59.500
There's going to be two levels, right?
It's like, what can I do that's crazy?
 
00:02:59.500 --> 00:03:03.000
And then when you realize it's all about the duos,
how do I enable my duo to do
 
00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:07.000
something crazy? What we're really excited to see
is people going into the theory crafting
 
00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:11.000
of figuring out what combinations work really well
and building their own agent and living
 
00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:14.500
up to that fantasy. I want to see the crazy plays.
 
00:03:14.500 --> 00:03:19.500
I feel like we had a lot of fun internally playtesting it,
but our players always surprised us.
 
00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:24.000
Also, do players like how messed up the game is?
You know, do players have other ways
 
00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:29.000
they want to be using other abilities, and what are those,
and how can we help deliver on that?
 
00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:33.500
I see it as almost our love letter
to our Valorant agents and their abilities.
 
00:03:33.500 --> 00:03:37.000
You know, we wanted to
 
00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:41.000
provide a way to experience them to the fullest
and really live up to that fantasy.
 
00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:44.000
And I really hope players get to enjoy that.
 
00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:48.000
Play the mode. Tell your friends about it.
Play it with your friends.
 
00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:52.000
Tell your parents. Tell everybody.
Just get everybody on to play Gauntlet Glitched,
 
00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:58.000
please, so we can keep working on it.
We'd love to make more for the mode.
 
